  "query_preview": "..\n(Friday night through next Wednesday)\nIssued at 1241 PM CDT Thu Oct 29 2026\n\nLow level easterly winds will remain in place through Friday night \ninto Saturday morning. Some model guidance is still showing some \nlingering precipitation off the caprock through Saturday morning. \nHowever, this is most likely low stratus and possibly drizzle. Short \nwave ridging will return late Saturday through the day on Sunday in \nadvance of the next trough digging into the western CONUS. The next \nshort wave trough will track to the four corners by Monday morning \nproviding another shot of precipitation from late Sunday through \nMonday. Forcing associated with this short wave looks to be briefer \nthan what is expected for Friday but also may be stronger. The other \nnotable feature in the long term forecast will be a strong cold \nfront currently forecast to move through on Tuesday morning. Surface \nwinds will pack a punch behind this front but temperatures don't \nappear to be significantly affected.",
